Efficiency and Real-World Application:
Nuclear fission is highly efficient for energy production, but it requires careful management of nuclear materials and poses challenges with radioactive waste disposal.

2. Nuclear Fusion: Fusing Atoms (Future Technology)

Nuclear fusion is the process that powers the sun and stars. It involves fusing two light atomic nuclei (typically hydrogen isotopes like deuterium and tritium) to form a heavier nucleus, releasing vast amounts of energy.

How it works:

Under extremely high pressure and temperature (like in the core of stars or in experimental fusion reactors), two hydrogen nuclei fuse to form a helium nucleus.

This fusion releases energy in the form of heat and high-energy particles.

Mass-Energy Conversion:
